index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..9a02cd7315659d1495c35f25f1b68c0a8bb3154b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/lmcache-t3knic/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# lmcache-t3knic
+
+`lmcache-t3knic` provides the LMCache 0.4.4 adapter and vLLM connector for
+cross-node KV-cache transfer between a Galaxy system and a T3K server.
+Calling `lmcache_t3knic.apply()` installs the small LMCache compatibility
+hooks required by the TT connector and registers it with vLLM.
+
+TTNN-dependent code is isolated under `lmcache_t3knic.t3knic_lmcache` and is
+imported lazily so plugin discovery does not initialize the TT runtime.
+`lmcache_t3knic.specs` remains free of any `ttnn` import at module scope.
+
+## TT-Metal integration
+
+The kvcache-manager patch series adds this package, the required TTNN
+operations, the KV-cache manager runtime, and static inter-mesh support to the
+pinned upstream TT-Metal revision. No separate TT-Metal fork is required.
+
+## Activation
+
+Install the package in the Python environment used by vLLM:
+
+```bash
+python -m pip install ./lmcache-t3knic
+```
+
+For a source checkout, add the package to `PYTHONPATH`:
+
+```bash
+export PYTHONPATH="${TT_METAL_ROOT}/lmcache-t3knic:${PYTHONPATH:-}"
+```
+
+Plain `import lmcache_t3knic` is intentionally side-effect free. Call
+`lmcache_t3knic.apply()` explicitly when using the package outside the vLLM
+plugin path.
+
+## Runtime Compatibility
+
+`apply()` sets `NUMBA_CACHE_DIR` to a writable temp directory when the variable
+is not already configured. LMCache may import numba-backed CPU helpers, and
+numba's default cache placement can target read-only package source directories
+in containers or source-checkout launches. Existing operator-provided
+`NUMBA_CACHE_DIR` values are left unchanged.
